lxml 6.1.3, for its cross build only: setupinfo.py runs pkg-config through the shell, and in cibuildwheel's
Android build environment CPython's subprocess runs shell commands with /system/bin/sh, which the build machine has
not. The command runs without a shell instead (its words split as the shell would). The built module is unchanged.

--- a/setupinfo.py
+++ b/setupinfo.py
@@ -360,7 +360,8 @@
     if args:
         cmd = ' '.join((cmd,) + args)
 
-    p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, shell=True,
+    import shlex
+    p = subprocess.Popen(shlex.split(cmd),
                          stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
     stdout_data, errors = p.communicate()
 
